{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792268368,"nonce":"iJbCl77QXOZIgV6ytmZzs/puC5A=","title":"Run through runtime profiles: ash and rayzor","message":"P3, part of 7050a1a. A project names a runtime profile: language server, build, run, reload. ash (default): build through the compilation server, run in hybrid mode with --hot-reload, recompile and reload on save (hl.Api.checkReload), AOT build with ash --build. rayzor (../rayzor, a Haxe compiler in Rust with tiered JIT, not ash-compatible): its CLI to build and run, and rayzor-lsp (Rust, stdio) as the language server. Both get a console with streamed output and stack traces linked to source.","files":null}]}